TOOLSURF — LEGAL NOTICE & AUTHORIZED USE POLICY
===================================================

ToolSurf is a security testing tool designed to identify vulnerabilities
in AI agent tool interfaces, including MCP servers, REST/OpenAPI endpoints,
GraphQL and gRPC services, A2A agents, OpenAI functions, and LangChain
tools. This tool is provided for AUTHORIZED SECURITY TESTING ONLY.

BY USING THIS SOFTWARE, YOU AGREE TO THE FOLLOWING:

1. AUTHORIZED TESTING ONLY
   You will only scan systems that you own, operate, or have explicit
   written authorization to test. Unauthorized scanning of third-party
   systems may violate the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA), the UK
   Computer Misuse Act, EU Directive 2013/40/EU, or equivalent laws in
   your jurisdiction.

2. RESPONSIBLE USE
   You will not use ToolSurf to:
   - Attack, disrupt, or damage systems you do not own or control
   - Exfiltrate data from systems without authorization
   - Develop exploits for malicious purposes
   - Bypass security controls on production systems without authorization

3. ACTIVE SCANNING
   Active modules make tool calls to the target. These calls may have side
   effects depending on the target's implementation, including writes,
   state changes, and outbound network requests. Only run active modules
   against systems you control, disposable test environments, or targets
   where you have explicit permission for active security testing.
   `full-active` mode is never appropriate for production targets you do
   not control.

4. ASSUMPTION OF RISK
